@startuml
title WF-01 Classroom Robot Allocation
|School Admin|
start
:Choose classroom and entitled robot;
|VISTA Web|
:GET eligible robots; PUT allocation;
|Education API|
:Authenticate and verify school_admin allocation permission;
if (Classroom organization and robot entitlement valid?) then (yes)
  |Database|
  :Upsert one allocation per classroom;
  |Education API|
  :Return safe robot projection;
  |Instructor|
  :Read authorized classroom and allocated robot;
else (no)
  :Return not found / authorization rejection;
endif
stop
@enduml

@startuml
title Classroom Lab Session (refines WF-01 allocation and the WF-03 start gate)
actor Instructor
actor Student
participant API as "Education API"
database DB as "PostgreSQL"
participant Edge as "Edge Runtime"
Instructor -> API : POST /classrooms/{id}/lab-sessions {robotId}
API -> DB : lock(robot); check allocation, entitlement, status, no open session, no active control
DB --> API : INSERT classroom_lab_sessions(active) [unique index = one open per robot]
API --> Instructor : active session (reserves only; no arming, no command)
Student -> API : start experiment
API -> DB : lock(robot); open session of THIS classroom? (else LAB_SESSION_NOT_ACTIVE / ROBOT_RESERVED_BY_ANOTHER_CLASSROOM)
API -> Edge : run command (existing MQTT/HTTP contract)
Instructor -> API : POST /lab-sessions/{id}/end
API -> DB : active -> terminating (no new runs)
API -> Edge : stop active run (R1 cancel) or wait for terminal event
alt no unfinished control session
  API -> DB : terminating -> released
else stop unconfirmed
  API -> DB : quarantined (robot stays blocked)
end
@enduml
